    "faq_detail_diy_TNTLEt": {
      "type": "faq-detail-diy",
      "blocks": {
        "item_fB4iUV": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/FAQS_3c69a52b-52ec-4567-8ec7-ce4a277cd176.jpg",
            "image1": "shopify://shop_images/FAQs-mobile_44504b31-28af-429c-95b5-6b0c4e93ea10.jpg",
            "title": "Can anyone use IPL?",
            "content": "<p>IPL (Intense Pulsed Light) hair removal works by emitting intense light pulses that are absorbed by the pigment in the hair follicles. The absorbed light is then converted into heat, which targets the hair follicles and inhibits future hair growth.<br/><br/>It is important to note that IPL is most effective on individuals with lighter skin tones and darker hair colors. This is because the light energy is primarily absorbed by the melanin pigment in the hair. In individual's skin that's rich in melanin, the excess melanin can also absorb the light energy, leading to potential skin damage.<br/><br/>Similarly, IPL may not be as effective on individuals with light hair colors such as blonde, gray, or red. This is because these hair colors have less melanin content, making it challenging for the IPL device to target the hair follicles effectively.<br/><br/>To ensure the effectiveness and safety of IPL hair removal, we recommend users refer to the our skin tone chart before making a purchase.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_LbhGqz": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Are Ulike IPL hair removal devices FDA-cleared?",
            "content": "<p>Yes, all our IPL hair removal devices are FDA-cleared, clinically tested, and compliant with international standards. We follow a comprehensive in-house development process that includes rigorous testing by international governing bodies. Ulike IPL devices have received over 30 global certifications, guaranteeing a reliable hair removal experience from start to finish.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_pwR4h8": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does IPL provide a long-lasting solution to hair removal?",
            "content": "<p>During the recommended 12-week treatment cycle, IPL (Intense Pulsed Light) targets the melanin within hair follicles, disrupting the growth cycle. This causes hair to grow back thinner and slower, eventually stopping altogether. Once you've achieved the desired results, you will need to perform monthly or bimonthly maintenance sessions to prevent regrowth.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_tDL4Fw": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How often should I use this product?",
            "content": "<p>We recommend using the device three times a week for the first month to achieve the best results. After that, you can use it once every two weeks or once a month for touch-ups as needed.<br/><br/>Furthermore, we advise tailoring your usage according to your hair growth. If you encounter areas with thicker hair or stubbornness, feel free to increase the intensity level and frequency of usage. Always pay attention to your skin's response and adjust accordingly to ensure your comfort and avoid any discomfort or adverse effects.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_qbgfTp": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do I have to shave before using Ulike IPL hair removal devices?",
            "content": "<p>Yes, it is recommended to shave any hair longer than 2 mm in the treated area. This ensures the IPL light can target the hair root directly without being obstructed by surface hair. Failure to shave may result in a burning smell during treatment caused by the IPL light burning surface hair stubble or residue instead of reaching the hair follicles. Use shaving alone to prepare the skin, as other methods remove the hair root and may reduce the treatment's effectiveness.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_ebRfyK": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How many times a week should I use Ulike IPL devices?",
            "content": "<p>IPL (Intense Pulsed Light) technology targets hair follicles during their anagen (growth) phase. Hairs in the same body area might not be in this phase simultaneously. In order to ensure each hair follicle is treated at least once during its active growth phase, we recommend a 12-week cycle: <strong>start with 3 treatments per week for 4 weeks, then switch to maintenance sessions once or twice a month.</strong> Additionally, tailor your treatment frequency to your hair growth patterns. For areas with thicker hair or stubborn growth, adjust the power level and frequency as needed. Always monitor your skin's response and make adjustments to prevent discomfort.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
